        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Ukraine's Zelensky pledges clear timetable of talks on EU membership Europe Issued on: 04/06/2026 - 21:39 Modified: 04/06/2026 - 21:42 President Volodymyr Zelensky ⁠pledged on Thursday that ​Ukraine would keep to a clear timetable in talks on joining the ​European Union and in sticking to its obligations with the 27-nation bloc. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Georgia's former minister of Euro-Atlantic integration and professor at SciencesPo Paris Tornike Gorgadze. Ukraine war and risk of stagnation hang over St Petersburg economic conference 04/06/2026 Europe Massive disinformation campaign underway in Armenia ahead of elections, analysts warn 04/06/2026 Europe A 'rogues' gallery' of notorious figures at Russia's biggest economic conference 04/06/2026 Europe Albania: luxury complex project linked to Trump's family sparks outrage 04/06/2026 Europe Ukraine pushed Russia back in May for second month running, ISW finds 03/06/2026 Europe Deadly attack on migrants highlights issue of labour abuse in Italy 03/06/2026 Europe UK far right exploiting student stabbing attack 'to promote moral panic', expert says 03/06/2026 Europe Ukraine's attack on Saint Petersburg 'brings war back to Russia' 03/06/2026 Europe Russia: Ukraine drones hit Saint Petersburg 03/06/2026 Europe"
