        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Massive disinformation campaign underway in Armenia ahead of elections, analysts warn Europe Issued on: 04/06/2026 - 21:05 One ballot box, two competing battles. In Armenia, voters are heading to the polls to decide the future direction of their country. But beneath the political campaigns lies a far more insidious warfare. Analysts warn that a massive, coordinated network of foreign disinformation - much of it tracing back to Russia - is systematically weaponizing the deep-seated trauma of recent wars. FRANCE 24's Olivia Bizot reports from Yerevan. A 'rogues' gallery' of notorious figures at Russia's biggest economic conference 04/06/2026 Europe Albania: luxury complex project linked to Trump's family sparks outrage 04/06/2026 Europe Ukraine pushed Russia back in May for second month running, ISW finds 03/06/2026 Europe Deadly attack on migrants highlights issue of labour abuse in Italy 03/06/2026 Europe UK far right exploiting student stabbing attack 'to promote moral panic', expert says 03/06/2026 Europe Ukraine's attack on Saint Petersburg 'brings war back to Russia' 03/06/2026 Europe Russia: Ukraine drones hit Saint Petersburg 03/06/2026 Europe Ukrainian drones hit Saint Petersburg as 'Russian Davos' opens in the city 03/06/2026 Europe UK: Outrage grows after police handcuff dying student 03/06/2026 Europe"
